  in published work. The software citation below identifies the archived version.
type: software
title: >-
  sensory-semantic-episodes: code for Replay builds a shared vocabulary between
  episodic and semantic memory that enhances recall and consolidation
authors:
  - family-names: Albesa Gonzalez
    given-names: Albert
    affiliation: Sainsbury Wellcome Centre
  - family-names: Clopath
    given-names: Claudia
    affiliation: Imperial College London
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24497226
repository-code: https://github.com/albesagonzalez/sensory-semantic-episodes
license: MIT
keywords:
  - systems consolidation
  - episodic memory
  - semantic memory
  - neural replay
  - computational neuroscience
abstract: >-
  Simulation and analysis code for a model of episodic-semantic memory
  interactions in which bidirectional replay establishes a shared vocabulary
  between medial temporal lobe and neocortex. The software includes the model,
  figure notebooks, parameter sweeps, plotting utilities, pinned dependencies,
  and a notebook execution runner.
